WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.601
Riya searches her college notice board for placement

2
00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:05.619
drive. Zero results. But the notice is right

3
00:00:05.654 --> 00:00:08.638
there: campus recruitment starts Monday.

4
00:00:08.988 --> 00:00:12.018
Keyword search matches letters, and these two phrases

5
00:00:12.053 --> 00:00:14.340
share no words. She needs a search that

6
00:00:14.398 --> 00:00:15.490
matches meaning.

7
00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:18.534
An embedding model does exactly that. Give it

8
00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:21.123
any text, and it returns a fixed-length list

9
00:00:21.169 --> 00:00:24.257
of numbers: for example, fifteen hundred and thirty-six

10
00:00:24.315 --> 00:00:25.360
of them.

11
00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:28.798
No single number means anything alone. Together, they

12
00:00:28.845 --> 00:00:31.085
work like coordinates: one point in a very

13
00:00:31.143 --> 00:00:32.444
large space.

14
00:00:32.794 --> 00:00:35.627
Here is that space, flattened to two dimensions.

15
00:00:36.045 --> 00:00:39.435
Placement drive lands right beside campus recruitment.

16
00:00:39.785 --> 00:00:42.664
Biryani recipe lands far away. The model was

17
00:00:42.711 --> 00:00:45.044
trained on huge numbers of text pairs, so

18
00:00:45.114 --> 00:00:47.448
close points mean similar things.

19
00:00:47.798 --> 00:00:50.492
Now Riya's search is simple: embed the query,

20
00:00:50.515 --> 00:00:52.674
and return the nearest points.

21
00:00:53.024 --> 00:00:55.485
The same idea powers RAG, and matching your

22
00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:57.575
resume to a job description.

23
00:00:57.925 --> 00:01:01.234
Two rules. First, embed documents and queries with

24
00:01:01.269 --> 00:01:03.904
the same model. Every model draws its own

25
00:01:03.962 --> 00:01:04.752
map.

26
00:01:05.102 --> 00:01:07.401
Second, similar is not the same as true.

27
00:01:07.819 --> 00:01:09.978
I love DSA and I hate DSA often

28
00:01:10.048 --> 00:01:11.557
land close together.

29
00:01:11.907 --> 00:01:14.310
So here's the line to remember: an embedding

30
00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:17.364
turns meaning into a position. Close together means

31
00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:18.734
similar meaning.

32
00:01:19.084 --> 00:01:22.753
Next lesson: cosine similarity from scratch with NumPy.
